    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=af17eb32-b7ad-4f2c-8d25-781ac5b31aa0&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201954048048_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Enrollment Communications and Digital Content Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-22\n\nLocation: Richmond\n\nEarlham College is a Top 100 National Liberal Arts College located in Richmond, IN, a small city that's just a short drive away from several major metropolitan areas including Dayton, Cincinnati, Indianapolis and Chicago. Richmond and Earlham have a symbiotic relationship. Through research, studies, internships and volunteering, Earlhamites offer Richmond expertise and service as Richmond offers our students the chance to gain valuable, real-world experience. Our community assumes no religious affiliation but follows Quaker principles and practices, which include respect for persons, integrity, a commitment to peace and justice, simplicity, and consensus-based community decision-making. Earlham is committed to and proud of being a diverse and inclusive place most clearly visible in our student body: 20% of our student body are international, coming from 60+ nations in 2022, and 24% are domestic students of color. Faculty and staff also bring tremendous diversity to the College; many have lived and worked outside the United States, and they make a point of drawing on those experiences in their interactions with students. Additionally, Earlham makes it a priority to serve as a safe and welcoming place for LGBTQ+ communities and has a four-star rating on the Campus Pride Index. Our community is characterized by respect for every person and a commitment to social justice. Equity and inclusion are central to Earlham's institutional priorities and our leadership is committed to widening the path to an Earlham education. Position Overview The Enrollment Communications and Digital Content Specialist manages day-to-day execution of our admissions communications program in Slate, working at the intersection of enrollment marketing, data, and content. This role pairs persuasive, on-brand storytelling with data-driven execution — building and testing email and SMS campaigns, maintaining the data dictionary and query library with our CRM captain, and keeping a reporting cadence with reliable attribution — continuously advising on how to optimize campaigns in service of our broader enrollment strategy, so senior staff can focus on funnel-wide direction and where digital marketing goes next. Beyond admissions communications, this person also makes recruitment-focused updates to website copy and manages requests from faculty and staff for email communications to families of current students. We're looking for someone who treats this as more than a queue of send requests: someone who looks at performance data and asks what to try next, flags friction points before they're raised, and brings ideas for testing, personalization, and refinement without waiting to be asked. This is a full-time, in-person role. Primary Duties & Responsibilities Email/SMS communication —  Build, deploy, and manage all Slate Deliver communications for admissions, including merge fields, Liquid markup for dynamic/conditional content, and population-based logic. Content and storytelling —  Draft persuasive, on-brand copy across email, SMS, and web that turns admissions and campus information into a compelling case for prospective students and families to act, partnering with counselors, faculty, and other stakeholders to keep it accurate and timely. Calendar and coordination —  Manage the admissions email communications calendar (prospect through enrollment/yield), coordinating timing with recruitment, financial aid, and events, and partnering with enrollment leadership so communications complement rather than duplicate counselor outreach. Digital content —  Keep website copy and recruitment communications aligned with the enrollment cycle and current recruitment initiatives and marketing campaigns, creating and updating content across both platforms as those priorities shift. Conversion optimization —  Look for ways to align content with the action we want a prospect to take next, flagging friction points and recommending improvements — including new or updated lead-generation ideas — based on campaign performance data. Quality assurance —  Test email and SMS sends for design, layout, and accurate Liquid markup rendering across devices and email clients before deployment. Data dictionary and segmentation —  Manage and expand the admissions data dictionary and supporting query library in coordination with the CRM/data team, maintaining segment definitions (scholarship eligibility, area of interest, distance from campus, engagement history, etc.) for accurate, personalized targeting. Testing and reporting —  Design and run a recurring A/B testing program on subject lines, send times, content, and CTAs, documenting results as institutional best practice. Establish and maintain a regular campaign performance reporting cadence — click-through rates, opt-out/spam rates, deliverability, conversions where possible (visit registrations, form submissions, etc) — with consistent UTM/source tracking for accurate attribution. Future focus — Pilot new tactics to build on current momentum and set us apart in the competitive landscape. Partner communications — Review content from our enrollment marketing partner and develop feedback and recommendations to keep messaging aligned with our brand and enrollment strategy.  Current-family communications —  Manage requests from faculty and staff for email communications to families of current students, ensuring timely, accurate, and on-brand messaging. Qualifications Required Bachelor's degree required A skilled, persuasive communicator with a strong command of brand voice and guidelines — able to turn admissions and campus information into compelling, action-oriented copy across email, web, and other channels, for audiences ranging from prospective students to families of current students. Experience building and managing email and/or SMS marketing campaigns; direct experience with Slate, or a comparable CRM/marketing automation platform. Comfort working with merge fields, conditional/dynamic content logic (e.g., Liquid markup), and query-based segmentation, or a demonstrated ability to learn these quickly. Experience with, or aptitude for, basic website content management and copywriting for a recruitment/marketing audience. An analytical mindset — comfort reading campaign performance data (A/B test results, funnel and conversion metrics) and drawing practical conclusions from it. Excellent organization and cross-functional collaboration skills; this role coordinates closely with recruitment, financial aid, events, faculty and staff, and an external marketing partner. A proactive, curious approach — someone who looks for what could be tested, personalized, or improved rather than waiting to be asked. Preferred Master's degree preferred Prior experience in higher education admissions or enrollment marketing. Working knowledge of HTML/CSS — comfortable editing code within email templates to add Liquid markup and show or hide content blocks without breaking the template's design or send. Experience building or maintaining a data dictionary or audience segmentation framework. To Apply Please submit the following materials with your application: Cover letter Resume List of Three References with Contact Information The review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Employee Benefits at Earlham Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance* Company paid Long-Term Disability after 1 year of full-time service* Basic and Voluntary Life insurance*  Employee Assistance Program* Campus Store Discount Free ticket vouchers for Richmond Symphony Orchestra Wellness Center Free Membership or Discount for eligible employees Athletic Games-Free entry to all home games  Free entry into most Theatre/Music shows Tuition Benefits for Immediate Family for eligible employees* 403(b) Retirement* – For eligible employees, Earlham will contribute a non-elective contribution equal to 5% of gross pay after 2 years of service. After 3 years of service, this non-elective contribution increases to 8%. Vesting credit is available for new employees with previous service in the education sector with required documentation. Many Wayne County Chamber of Commerce member businesses offer discounts to anyone with an Earlham ID *All employee benefit offerings are subject to employee eligibility per plan documents.  Earlham College is an equal opportunity employer and prohibits discrimination against any individual based on race, color, national origin, gender, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, disability, veteran status, genetic information, religion, or other protected classifications under applicable laws. The College is committed to building a diverse community that reflects the makeup of society and particularly welcomes and supports individuals from historically marginalized groups. As an institution with a Quaker identity, Earlham also encourages applications from members of the Religious Society of Friends (Quakers). Earlham College complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) and applicable state law. If you are an individual with a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to perform the essential functions of the position, or to participate in the hiring process, please contact the Earlham College Office of Human Resources. Earlham's Work Authorization Policy Earlham utilizes   E-Verify   to confirm employment eligibility for all newly hired employees within the United States. \n Monday – Friday, 8:00am – 5:00pm Full-time, Admin Faculty, 40 hours per week",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=af17eb32-b7ad-4f2c-8d25-781ac5b31aa0&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201954059658_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Graphic and Multimedia Designer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-22\n\nLocation: Richmond\n\nEarlha m College is a Top 100 National Liberal Arts College located in Richmond, IN, a small city that's just a short drive away from several major metropolitan areas including Dayton, Cincinnati, Indianapolis and Chicago. Richmond and Earlham have a symbiotic relationship. Through research, studies, internships and volunteering, Earlhamites offer Richmond expertise and service as Richmond offers our students the chance to gain valuable, real-world experience. Our community assumes no religious affiliation but follows Quaker principles and practices, which include respect for persons, integrity, a commitment to peace and justice, simplicity, and consensus-based community decision-making. Earlham is committed to and proud of being a diverse and inclusive place most clearly visible in our student body: 20% of our student body are international, coming from 60+ nations in 2022, and 24% are domestic students of color. Faculty and staff also bring tremendous diversity to the College; many have lived and worked outside the United States, and they make a point of drawing on those experiences in their interactions with students. Additionally, Earlham makes it a priority to serve as a safe and welcoming place for LGBTQ+ communities and has a four-star rating on the Campus Pride Index. Our community is characterized by respect for every person and a commitment to social justice. Equity and inclusion are central to Earlham's institutional priorities and our leadership is committed to widening the path to an Earlham education. Position Overview The Graphic and Multimedia Designer translates concepts and themes into compelling and brand-appropriate visual design of print materials and digital media. Highly creative and original, the Graphic and Multimedia Designer is a key member of the Marketing and Communications team who brings energy and ideas to each new endeavor. With a track record of producing high-quality, innovative materials and a wealth of knowledge about emerging design practices and production processes, the Graphic and Multimedia Designer is able to propose solutions that delight clients and elevate the Earlham brand.  This position reports to the Senior Creative Director/Project Manager , and is part of a highly collaborative, multifunctional marketing and communications team that includes writing and editing, design, photo, video, web development and marketing strategy.  Primary Duties & Responsibilities Meeting clients or account managers to discuss the project objectives and requirements of the job Estimating the time required to complete the work Thinking creatively to produce new ideas and concepts and developing compelling design Using innovation to redefine a design brief within the constraints of cost and time Presenting finalized ideas and concepts to clients; Working with a range of media and keeping up to date with emerging technologies Develop creative concepts and visual designs for print and digital materials such as brochures, postcards, advertisements, alumni magazine, presentations, social media graphics, promotional materials, email marketing, and video projects. Produce video and multimedia content, including planning, basic camera/audio operation, editing, captioning and formatting content for web, social media and other digital channels. Proofreading to produce accurate and high-quality work Coordinate with vendors and prepare files for print production and digital distribution Working as part of a team with printers, copywriters, photographers, illustrators, other designers, web developers and marketing specialists Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree and 3-5 years experience required Proficiency in Adobe Creative Cloud, particularly InDesign, Illustrator, and Photoshop. Ideally experience in Adobe Premiere for video editing Passion and enthusiasm for design, with a creative flair A flexible approach when working in a team Communication skills: Able to meet with clients or the Senior Creative Director and Project Manager to determine the scope of a project and interpret and negotiate briefs with clients Good presentation skills and the confidence to explain and sell ideas to clients and colleagues  Time management skills and the ability to cope with several projects at a time Accuracy and attention to detail when finalizing designs Being open to feedback and willing to make changes to designs Review designs for errors before printing or publishing them Develop and maintain brand standards, templates, and visual assets for the campus community To Apply Please submit the following materials with your application: Cover letter  Resume List of Three References with Contact Information  The review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Employee Benefits at Earlham Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance* Company paid Long-Term Disability after 1 year of full-time service* Basic and Voluntary Life insurance*  Employee Assistance Program* Campus Store Discount Free ticket vouchers for Richmond Symphony Orchestra Wellness Center Free Membership or Discount for eligible employees Athletic Games-Free entry to all home games  Free entry into most Theatre/Music shows Tuition Benefits for Immediate Family for eligible employees* 403(b) Retirement* – For eligible employees, Earlham will contribute a non-elective contribution equal to 5% of gross pay after 2 years of service. After 3 years of service, this non-elective contribution increases to 8%. Vesting credit is available for new employees with previous service in the education sector with required documentation. Many Wayne County Chamber of Commerce member businesses offer discounts to anyone with an Earlham ID *All employee benefit offerings are subject to employee eligibility per plan documents.  Earlham College is an equal opportunity employer and prohibits discrimination against any individual based on race, color, national origin, gender, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, disability, veteran status, genetic information, religion, or other protected classifications under applicable laws. The College is committed to building a diverse community that reflects the makeup of society and particularly welcomes and supports individuals from historically marginalized groups. As an institution with a Quaker identity, Earlham also encourages applications from members of the Religious Society of Friends (Quakers). Earlham College complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) and applicable state law. If you are an individual with a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to perform the essential functions of the position, or to participate in the hiring process, please contact the Earlham College Office of Human Resources. Earlham's Work Authorization Policy Earlham utilizes   E-Verify   to confirm employment eligibility for all newly hired employees within the United States. \n Monday – Friday, 8:00am – 5:00pm Full-time, Admin Faculty, 40 hours per week",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=af17eb32-b7ad-4f2c-8d25-781ac5b31aa0&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201938752854_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Student Success Librarian",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-18\n\nLocation: Richmond\n\nEarlham College is a Top 100 National Liberal Arts College located in Richmond, IN, a small city that's just a short drive away from several major metropolitan areas including Dayton, Cincinnati, Indianapolis and Chicago. Richmond and Earlham have a symbiotic relationship. Through research, studies, internships and volunteering, Earlhamites offer Richmond expertise and service as Richmond offers our students the chance to gain valuable, real-world experience. Our community assumes no religious affiliation but follows Quaker principles and practices, which include respect for persons, integrity, a commitment to peace and justice, simplicity, and consensus-based community decision-making. Earlham is committed to and proud of being a diverse and inclusive place most clearly visible in our student body: 20% of our student body are international, coming from 60+ nations in 2022, and 24% are domestic students of color. Faculty and staff also bring tremendous diversity to the College; many have lived and worked outside the United States, and they make a point of drawing on those experiences in their interactions with students. Additionally, Earlham makes it a priority to serve as a safe and welcoming place for LGBTQ+ communities and has a four-star rating on the Campus Pride Index. Our community is characterized by respect for every person and a commitment to social justice. Equity and inclusion are central to Earlham's institutional priorities and our leadership is committed to widening the path to an Earlham education. Position Overview  The Student Success Librarian is focused on instruction, outreach, programing & partnerships for the library. The Student Success Librarian is a primary point of direct library and research support for students and faculty across the campus.  Primary Duties & Responsibilities Instruction  Design, teach, and assess course-integrated information literacy sessions in collaboration with faculty to infuse critical thinking and research fluency throughout the curriculum.  Teach in LIFT, the library's credit-bearing first-year program for first-generation college students.  Teach AI literacy — how generative AI tools work, where they fail, how to evaluate their output, and how to use them ethically in academic work. Audiences include students and employees.  Support media and multimodal assignments with options including podcasting, video and audio editing, infographic design, and poster design for students presenting at Epic Expo and the Academic Fair.  Provide individual research consultations to Earlham students, in person and online; answer reference questions from students, employees, and the wider community; and administer the library's chat support service.  Outreach  Conduct vigorous library outreach with campus faculty, students, and staff. Build relationships that bring students into the library, and foster a sense of belonging.  Run the library's social media presence and promotional communications.  Serve as a library liaison to select academic departments and programs. Select materials for assigned areas.  Administer the library's web presence through LibGuides. Create, maintain, review, and retire research and course guides; and lead the remediation project bringing library digital content into conformance with WCAG 2.1 AA standards ahead of the April 2027 federal deadline.  Coordinate with library colleagues to optimize database and discovery interfaces and troubleshoot user-reported problems.  Programming & Partnerships  Plan and organize library programming. Coordinate with partners for campus-wide events like New Student Orientation, Earlham Day, and Epic Expo.  Partner closely with colleagues in the Library, Information Technology Services, and the Academic Enrichment Center to align student support across the building and to build shared referral pathways.  Partner with campus student success units, including academic advising, the Center for Global and Career Education, the McNair Program, and other departments.  Represent Earlham in PALNI (Private Academic Library Network of Indiana) working groups and collaborative initiatives. Participate in consortial and professional communities relevant to the position.  Additional duties as assigned.  Qualifications A Master's degree in library/information science, or a related field, required.  Experience in higher education settings, preferred.  Teaching experience, in a library or another educational setting, preferred.  Interest in or experience with generative AI tools in teaching, research support, or professional development, preferred.  Familiarity with web accessibility standards (WCAG, Section 508), preferred.  Experience with LibGuides, content management systems, or web editing, preferred.  Knowledge of trends in academic libraries, preferred.  To Apply Please submit the following materials with your application: Cover letter Resume List of Three References with Contact Information  The review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Employee Benefits at Earlham Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance* Company paid Long-Term Disability after 1 year of full-time service* Basic and Voluntary Life insurance*  Employee Assistance Program* Campus Store Discount Free ticket vouchers for Richmond Symphony Orchestra Wellness Center Free Membership or Discount for eligible employees Athletic Games-Free entry to all home games  Free entry into most Theatre/Music shows Tuition Benefits for Immediate Family for eligible employees* 403(b) Retirement* – For eligible employees, Earlham will contribute a non-elective contribution equal to 5% of gross pay after 2 years of service. After 3 years of service, this non-elective contribution increases to 8%. Vesting credit is available for new employees with previous service in the education sector with required documentation. Many Wayne County Chamber of Commerce member businesses offer discounts to anyone with an Earlham ID *All employee benefit offerings are subject to employee eligibility per plan documents.  Earlham College is an equal opportunity employer and prohibits discrimination against any individual based on race, color, national origin, gender, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, disability, veteran status, genetic information, religion, or other protected classifications under applicable laws. The College is committed to building a diverse community that reflects the makeup of society and particularly welcomes and supports individuals from historically marginalized groups. As an institution with a Quaker identity, Earlham also encourages applications from members of the Religious Society of Friends (Quakers). Earlham College complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) and applicable state law. If you are an individual with a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to perform the essential functions of the position, or to participate in the hiring process, please contact the Earlham College Office of Human Resources. Earlham's Work Authorization Policy Earlham utilizes  E-Verify  to confirm employment eligibility for all newly hired employees within the United States.",
